@@ -0,0 +1,70 @@
+\ The layout of the space of the emulator for the definitions on the host (18.19; design 7.2.15, 7.2.17, 7.2.24).
+\ The language lays everything the emulator does for a definition on the host: where the number of a definition goes (the
+\ "processor" of the host), where the arguments lie, where the program positions of the results are given. This text
+\ is the only place of the layout. The compiler reads these constants to compile a call (primitives.fth); at the
+\ build tools/host_layout.py executes the same text on the host pForth and writes the constants as
+\ emulator/src/host_layout.h (HL_...), the table that the emulator (the code of the definitions: C) reads and writes
+\ by, and nothing else. Only constants: the names are the names of C macros (upper case, - as _).
+\ A call is one long copy (15.2) into the space of the emulator: the record of the long copy (HL-REC bits: op, space,
+\ flags, length, position) and right after it the bits of the block of the call, written at the position HL-PROC of
+\ the space of the emulator. The processor of the host is the cell of 32 bits at HL-PROC: the emulator looks at it
+\ after every copy into its space, and a number there is a call of the definition of that number (the cell is
+\ cleared). The places below (HL-RET, HL-IMG, the arguments, the ends) are bits from HL-PROC, that is from the start
+\ of the block of the call: the cells HL-IMG (the position of the program for the image the definition makes) and
+\ HL-RET (for its 32-bit return value) tell the emulator where to copy the results.
+4096 constant hl-space      \ the number of the space of the emulator in the long copy (0 SYS, 1 the clock, 2.. files)
+0 constant hl-proc          \ the processor of the host: the position (bits) of its cell of 32 bits, the start of a block of a call
+8192 constant hl-in         \ the bits of the space of the emulator that a copy may write (the calls)
+8192 constant hl-out        \ the position of the image that a definition makes (the area of the results)
+8388608 constant hl-out-bits \ the bits of the area of the image
+152 constant hl-rec          \ the record of the long copy (proto.def: op 8, chan 32, flags 16, arg 32, off 64)
+\ The numbers of the definitions (not zero; under 16: the tables of the compiler, forthc.fth).
+1 constant hl-clash-n   2 constant hl-fill-n    3 constant hl-enc-n
+4 constant hl-add-n     5 constant hl-sub-n     6 constant hl-and-n     7 constant hl-or-n
+8 constant hl-xor-n     9 constant hl-eq-n     10 constant hl-lt-n     11 constant hl-ult-n
+12 constant hl-put-n   13 constant hl-cmove-n  14 constant hl-num-n
+\ The results: the cells the call gives (32 bits numeric, the position in the space of the program, in bits), then
+\ the arguments from HL-ARGS (the number of the definition is the cell at 0). A block of the call is in the memory of the program: the record and the cells; an
+\ array of the memory that the call carries lies right after the block, at a slot of 64 bits.
+32 constant hl-ret
+64 constant hl-img
+96 constant hl-args
+\ clashes ( size, new row, layer record ): the size, the four cells of the new row, the record of the layer (the
+\ cell, the next, the count n, from the cell 3 the rows of four cells)
+hl-args constant hl-clash-size
+hl-clash-size 32 + hl-rec + 63 + 6 rshift constant hl-clash-cells
+hl-clash-cells 6 lshift hl-rec - constant hl-clash-row
+hl-clash-row 256 + constant hl-clash-layer
+hl-clash-layer 1984 + constant hl-clash-end
+\ fill ( u, c, r = the two low bits of the address )
+hl-args constant hl-fill-u
+hl-args 32 + constant hl-fill-c
+hl-args 64 + constant hl-fill-r
+hl-fill-r 32 + constant hl-fill-end
+hl-fill-end hl-rec + 63 + 6 rshift constant hl-fill-cells
+\ encode of a layer ( a, slots, count, the rows lay-rows: four cells each )
+hl-args constant hl-enc-a
+hl-args 32 + constant hl-enc-slots
+hl-args 64 + constant hl-enc-count
+hl-enc-count 32 + hl-rec + 63 + 6 rshift constant hl-enc-cells
+hl-enc-cells 6 lshift hl-rec - constant hl-enc-rows
+hl-enc-rows 2016 + constant hl-enc-end
+\ the binary words + - and or xor = < u< ( a b )
+hl-args constant hl-bin-a
+hl-args 32 + constant hl-bin-b
+hl-bin-b 32 + constant hl-bin-end
+hl-bin-end hl-rec + 63 + 6 rshift constant hl-bin-cells
+\ put and cmove ( n, rs and rd = the two low bits of the addresses of the source and of the destination, the 33
+\ slots of the memory of the source from the slot of its address )
+hl-args constant hl-mv-n
+hl-args 32 + constant hl-mv-rs
+hl-args 64 + constant hl-mv-rd
+hl-args 96 + constant hl-mv-src
+hl-mv-src 2112 + constant hl-mv-end
+hl-mv-end hl-rec + 63 + 6 rshift constant hl-mv-cells
+\ numeric ( the value, the number of bytes, rd )
+hl-args constant hl-num-v
+hl-args 32 + constant hl-num-nb
+hl-args 64 + constant hl-num-rd
+hl-num-rd 32 + constant hl-num-end
+hl-num-end hl-rec + 63 + 6 rshift constant hl-num-cells
